---
// A cheese named for how sharp it is, and the dish that needs it.
---

<p>
	Räßkäse is my favourite cheese so I'm including it in this list as notable. Power abuse? Perhaps.
</p>
<p>
	It's a very sharp, pungeant and amazingly flavourful cheese and it's a dish on its own — it goes best on a piece of rye bread with a bit of butter, pepper, and nothing else. You can find it in specialty cheese shops in Austria.
</p>